:: Carter Hang Out Park Playground Basic [nobr]

/* Intro */
As expected, when you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> what he would like to play, he suggests the two of you be superheroes. <span style="color:lightgreen">You laugh at this expected suggestion and agree to ‘play’ superheroes with him when <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> chuckles curiously.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Play? No, no, my dear sidekick! You misunderstand! Follow me!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> dashes forward towards the bushes and you follow with an amused expression. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
        {
        Name: "Carter",
        State: {
            Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
            Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

He takes you through the entire outline of the playground until you come across the swing set. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“There!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> points to it. You peek out and see… not much. <span style="color:yellow">The swing set is empty save for a larger gentleman sitting on the center swing clicking away on his phone.</span> You don’t understand and tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> as such. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No worries, my dependable sidekick, for I have already gathered all the information we need! You see, since we arrived, I’ve kept my eyes peeled for trouble and sensed it from this man. I thought I was mistaken, until I saw- Gasp! Look!”</span> You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> if he really just said the word ‘gasp’, but he tells you to just look. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:yellow">Over by the swings, a pair of younger kids walks over to get on, but as soon as they get close the older man begins to shout and yell at them. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fuck off brats! I was here first and I don’t want to see your dumb ass faces!”</span> The kids try to argue, but the larger man threats to pound them, so they run off. You suddenly get what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is talking about. This jerk is hogging the entire swing set and he’s not even using it right! This is a job for a pair of heroes, but what are you going to do?</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Simple.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says with a confident smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m going to walk over there and give him a piece of my mind! And, should the need arise, give him a butt whooping he won’t soon forget!”</span> Your friend poses heroically as you look between <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, <span style="color:Pink">a skinny little boy with sagging shorts who needs a booster seat to see out the car window,</span> and the large man, <span style="color:yellow">who is as thick as a tree and nearly as tall as one. You tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> that this is probably a VERY bad idea, but he brushes you off.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nonsense! The bigger they are, the harder they fall!”</span> <br>
<br>
You try to convince <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> that this, really, is a bad idea, but he begins to march over there. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey you!”</span> He calls out, stopping in front of the man in a heroic pose. The man glances up from his phone and growls for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fuck off!”</span> but the little hero stands his ground. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Just who do you think you are? You can’t hog the entire swing set! There are 5 seats and you only need one, so you better stop being such a bully or else!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or else?”</span> The man chuckles, standing up so he is towering over the young lad. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or else what?”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
        Name: "Carter",
        State: {
            Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or else… or else I’ll…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> ponders for a minute, <span style="color:yellow">looking a little nervous,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or else I’ll go tell the proper authorities and- Ah!”</span> <span style="color:lightcoral"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> cries out as the man suddenly grabs <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s shirt, pulls it up over his head to blind him, and shoves him to the ground. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> tries to stand up, but as the dude sits back down on the swing, he places both of his large feet on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s back, pinning the weak boy on the ground! This leaves <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> in the sand blinded by his own shirt and trapped by the guy’s weight.</span> <br>
<br>
Utterly defeated. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:yellow">Well, guess it’s your turn to try something. But what to do?</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Mud attack!<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You think fast, spying a pool of mud nearby and bend down to get a nice big glob of it. <span style="color:yellow">The wet dirt mixed with some bunches of grass and a worm or two is the perfect projectile to teach that jerk a lesson. You pack it into a nice, tight ball before walking up, holding your hand cradling the ball behind your back.</span> You stand tall, sure to make <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> proud, and tell the bully to release your friend and get out of here or else! <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Another one?”</span> The guy looks annoyed, kicking <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> away and standing up. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly fixes his shirt and scrambles over to you to help you fight, though looks more than a little nervous. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You little brats want to play? Fine. I’ll shove you both headfirst into the toilet stalls, see if you’ll want to talk shit after that!”</span> You smile, telling the guy that the only brat here is him, which is ironic. <span style="color:lightgreen">Considering he is a grown man hogging playground equipment and picking fights with middle schoolers! How pathetic!</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The fuck you say!?”</span> This has the desired effect, as the man’s face turns red with anger! Suddenly, he yells out and runs towards you both. <span style="color:lightgreen">You grab <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s arm with your free hand and, right as the man is close enough to ensure impact and has his mouth open wide from yelling, you toss the mud ball as hard as you can directly at his face!</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:lightgreen">Most of it ends up in his mouth, the dirty, wet, worm-filled attack coating his tongue as the man quickly falls to the ground, gagging and spitting out the disgusting concoction.</span> You quickly turn to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and tell him to run, taking off and dragging the surprised boy away! <br>
        <br>
        Once you are hidden and sure the man didn’t see where you ran off to, <span style="color:lightgreen">you both peek out to see the bully running off, looking sick and still covered in mud. The two kids he yelled at before point and laugh then run over to the now empty swings. Mission accomplished!</span> <br>
        
        <<set _ad to [
            {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                Mouth: "Happy",
                Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh my gosh!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says with glee, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That was awesome! I didn’t know you had mud powers! Aaahhh! That. Was. So. Epic!”</span> <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> jumps up and down, looking positively ecstatic that you managed to beat the villain. You take in his praise with a smile, repeating one of his heroic speeches you’ve heard before about how good will always win over evil, or something like that. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> couldn’t be happier.</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:red">-Carter Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 5>>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Water attack!<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Looking around for some sort of method of attack or weapon, you spy a curious sight. A discarded paper cup sitting by the water fountain. <span style="color:lightgreen">It gives you a devious idea as you run over and fill the cup up with as much icy cold water as you can! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> struggles against the man but has no hope of escaping. Still, his struggles keep the man’s attention as he shouts for his footrest to stay still and occasionally kicks the boy. This just makes you more upset, so you decide to add some ‘surprises’ to the water as well.</span> <br>
        <br>
        Then, you quietly begin to sneak over to the back of the boy, cup of cold water and other mystery ingredients in both hands as you try your best not to spill any, as you want it all to be saved for this jerk. <span style="color:lightgreen">Once you are close enough, you steady yourself before attacking-!</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:lightgreen">In one quick motion, you open up the back of the man’s shirt and pour the entire cup down his back! The icy liquid, mixed with whatever else you put into it, instantly soaks his shirt and pants, leading the man to let out a high-pitched scream! He falls to the ground in shock, utterly confused by what happened. You take this chance to run up to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, grabbing him, and take off running with his shirt still over his head!</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>? What happened!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> asks as the man, now realizing what had occurred, turns red with rage and gives chase! <span style="color:lightgreen">Thankfully, the large man isn’t the fastest, especially with a wet backside, and you are able to lose him and hide under the table of some very confused picnickers.</span> You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> spy on the man from the distance, who angrily calls out for you to come out and accept your ass whooping. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:lightgreen">Thankfully, either due to the uncomfortable wet clothes or the strange looks people are giving him, the man eventually decides to leave, still enraged.</span> Once he is gone, you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> crawl out of your hiding space and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> asks for a recap of what on earth happened! <br>
        
        <<set _ad to [
            {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                Mouth: "Happy",
                Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That. Was. So. Epic!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He says, jumping up and down with excitement as you recount your attack.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“A water attack! I should have thought of that! Haha, that’ll show him that evil never prevails!”</span> <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> laughs heroically, posing next to you.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You really are the best sidekick a hero could ask for!”</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:red">-Carter Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 5>>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>